      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "To a stirred solution of H4L (0.083 g, 0.2 mmol) and NEt3 (0.60 mL, 0.4 mmol) in MeOH (20 mL), Mn(ClO4)2·6H2O (0.072 g, 0.2 mmol) was added. Y(NO3)3·6H2O (0.076 g, 0.2 mmol) was then added. After stirring for 15 min, NaN3 (0.026 g, 0.4 mmol) was added and the mixture was stirred for a further 1 h. The brown solution was filtered. Purple platelet single crystals formed by slow evaporation of the filtrate over 2 days. NEt3 acts as a proton acceptor and provides basic conditions that facilitate aerial oxidation of MnII to MnIII.",
        "reagents": [
          {
            "name": "H4L (N,N'-dihydroxyethyl-N,N'-(2-hydroxy-4,5-dimethylbenzyl)ethylenediamine)",
